      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A yellow-coloured, Gram-stain-negative, non-motile, rod-shaped, strictly aerobic bacterium, designated 1-116T, was isolated from Erdos grassland soil of Inner Mongolia, PR China. Phylogenetic analysis based on 16S rRNA genes showed that strain 1-116T was a member of family Chitinophagaceae and exhibited the highest similarities to Taibaiella koreensis THG-DT86T (90.1\u200a%) and Flavihumibacter solisivae 3-3T (90.0\u200a%), while the similarities to the other Chitinophagaceae type strains were lower than 90.0\u200a%. Strain 1-116T grew at 16-33\u2009°C (optimum 28\u2009°C), pH 6.0-9.0 (optimum 7.0-8.0) and 0-0.5\u200a%\u2009NaCl (w/v; optimum without NaCl). A flexirubin-type pigment was present. The DNA G+C\u2009content was 43.2\u2009mol% and the only quinone present was menaquinone-7. The only polyamine detected was sym-homospermidine [30.7 µmol (g dry weight)-1] and the predominant fatty acids were iso-C15\u200a:\u200a0 (20.8\u200a%), iso-C15\u200a:\u200a1 G (25.1\u200a%), summed feature 4 (anteiso-C17\u200a:\u200a1 B and/or iso-C17\u200a:\u200a1 I; 13.8\u200a%) and iso-C17\u200a:\u200a0 3-OH (13.2\u200a%). The major polar lipids were phosphatidylethanolamine, three unidentified lipids, an unidentified aminophospholipid and an unidentified glycolipid. On the basis of the polyphasic analyses, strain 1-116T represents a novel genus and species in the family Chitinophagaceae, for which the name Edaphobaculum flavum gen. nov., sp. nov., is proposed. The type strain of Edaphobaculum flavum is 1-116T (=CCTCC\u2009AB 2017054=KCTC 52843)."},
